{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 3D Vision \u2014 Point Clouds & NeRFs Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: PointNet classifier"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class PointNet(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, num_classes=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mlp1 = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv1d(3, 64, 1),    nn.BatchNorm1d(64),   nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv1d(64, 64, 1),   nn.BatchNorm1d(64),   nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mlp2 = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv1d(64, 128, 1),  nn.BatchNorm1d(128),  nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv1d(128, 1024, 1), nn.BatchNorm1d(1024), nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(1024, 512),   nn.BatchNorm1d(512),  nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Dropout(0.3),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(512, 256),    nn.BatchNorm1d(256),  nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Dropout(0.3),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(256, num_classes),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # x: (N, 3, num_points) \u2014 transposed for Conv1d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.mlp1(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.mlp2(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = torch.max(x, dim=-1)[0]       # (N, 1024)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.head(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pts = torch.randn(4, 3, 1024)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "net = PointNet(num_classes=10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"output: {net(pts).shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"params: {sum(p.numel() for p in net.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "About 1.6M parameters. Runs on 1,024 points per cloud."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Positional encoding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def positional_encoding(x, L=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x: (..., D) -> (..., D * 2 * L)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    freqs = 2.0 ** torch.arange(L, dtype=x.dtype, device=x.device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    args = x.unsqueeze(-1) * freqs * 3.141592653589793"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sinc = torch.cat([args.sin(), args.cos()], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sinc.reshape(*x.shape[:-1], -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(5, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "y = positional_encoding(x, L=10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"input:  {x.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"encoded: {y.shape}     # (5, 60)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Multiplying by `2^l * pi` gives progressively higher frequencies."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Tiny NeRF MLP"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TinyNeRF(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, L_pos=10, L_dir=4, hidden=128):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.L_pos = L_pos"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.L_dir = L_dir"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pos_dim = 3 * 2 * L_pos"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        dir_dim = 3 * 2 * L_dir"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.trunk = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(pos_dim, hidden), nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(hidden, hidden),  nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(hidden, hidden),  nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(hidden, hidden),  nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.sigma = nn.Linear(hidden, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.color = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(hidden + dir_dim, hidden // 2), nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(hidden // 2, 3), nn.Sigmoid(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x, d):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x_enc = positional_encoding(x, self.L_pos)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        d_enc = positional_encoding(d, self.L_dir)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h = self.trunk(x_enc)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sigma = torch.relu(self.sigma(h)).squeeze(-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rgb = self.color(torch.cat([h, d_enc], dim=-1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return sigma, rgb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nerf = TinyNeRF()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(128, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "d = torch.randn(128, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "s, c = nerf(x, d)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"sigma: {s.shape}   rgb: {c.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Tiny compared to the original NeRF (which has 2 MLP trunks of depth 8). Enough to demonstrate the architecture."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Volumetric rendering along a ray"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def volumetric_render(sigma, rgb, t_vals):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sigma: (..., N_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rgb:   (..., N_samples, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t_vals: (N_samples,) distances along the ray"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    delta = torch.cat([t_vals[1:] - t_vals[:-1], torch.full_like(t_vals[:1], 1e10)])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    alpha = 1.0 - torch.exp(-sigma * delta)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    trans = torch.cumprod(torch.cat([torch.ones_like(alpha[..., :1]), 1.0 - alpha + 1e-10], dim=-1), dim=-1)[..., :-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    weights = alpha * trans"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rendered = (weights.unsqueeze(-1) * rgb).sum(dim=-2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    depth = (weights * t_vals).sum(dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return rendered, depth, weights"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "N = 64"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "t_vals = torch.linspace(2.0, 6.0, N)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sigma = torch.rand(N) * 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rgb = torch.rand(N, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rendered, depth, weights = volumetric_render(sigma, rgb, t_vals)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"rendered colour: {rendered.tolist()}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"depth:           {depth.item():.2f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One ray, 64 samples, composite to a single RGB pixel and a depth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Show that PointNet is permutation-invariant: run the same cloud through twice, once with points shuffled. Verify outputs are identical up to floating-point noise.\n2. **(Medium)** Implement a minimal ray-generation function that, given camera intrinsics and pose, produces ray origins and directions for every pixel of an H x W image.\n3. **(Hard)** Train a TinyNeRF on a synthetic dataset of rendered views of a coloured cube (generated via differentiable rendering or a simple ray tracer). Report rendering loss at epoch 1, 10, and 100. At what epoch does the model produce recognisable views?"
      ]
    }
